## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical handling of retries, deduplication, and observability in a common serverless ELT setup. It prompts decision between DLQ patterns and concrete idempotency strategy.

## Key Concepts
- Idempotent writes with deterministic IDs
- Dead-letter queues: Lambda DLQ vs SQS DLQ
- Observability: metrics, alarms, and alerting
- Minimal tooling: DynamoDB for seen IDs, CloudWatch for alerts

## Code Example
```javascript
// Lambda pseudo-code (Node.js)
const AWS = require('aws-sdk');
const ddb = new AWS.DynamoDB.DocumentClient();
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  for (const rec of event.Records) {
    const body = JSON.parse(rec.body); // or rec.kinesis, etc.
    const id = `${rec.s3.object.key}:${body.recordId}`;
    // Idempotency: check or upsert
    const exists = await ddb.get({TableName:'SeenIds', Key:{id}}).promise();
    if (exists.Item) continue;
    await ddb.put({TableName:'SeenIds', Item:{id}}).promise();
    // transform and write to target bucket
    // ... write CSV to target bucket
  }
  return {status: 'done'};
};
```

